# @ghbounty/db — environment variables
#
# This file is committed to git as documentation. Copy it to .env.local
# (NOT .env — .env.local is gitignored and is the convention used elsewhere
# in this repo, e.g. frontend/.env.local) and fill in the real values.
#
#   cp packages/db/.env.example packages/db/.env.local
#
# How to get DATABASE_URL from Supabase
# -------------------------------------
# 1. Open Supabase Studio for the project (devnet or prod).
# 2. Project Settings → Database → "Connection string" → URI tab.
# 3. Copy the URI. Format:
#      postgresql://postgres.<project_ref>:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres
#    Use the "Session pooler" connection (port 5432) for migrations —
#    NOT the "Transaction pooler" (port 6543), which doesn't support
#    schema-changing statements over multiple statements in one BEGIN block.
# 4. Replace `[YOUR-PASSWORD]` (or whatever placeholder Supabase shows)
#    with the real DB password. The password is set under the same Database
#    settings panel — "Database password". If you don't have it saved, you can
#    reset it (it does NOT log users out; only affects direct Postgres clients).
#
# Used by: drizzle-kit migrate, drizzle-kit push, drizzle-kit studio.
# NEVER commit a populated value to git.
DATABASE_URL=
